From e8041fd97c087bfa09b6c446935a62e525c45565 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chiro <chiro2001@163.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 22:20:06 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 140/257] feat(pypto-x): add native SVE256 W8A8 widening path

Implement contract 0002 C5 / R6 for the SVE256 backend:

- qmatmul_s8s8_s32 executes inside the AArch64 ELF with the native
  widening fallback: int8 lanes are sign-extended in two sunpklo steps
  (s8 -> s16 -> s32) and accumulated with integer mla.  No SDOT (SVE2)
  and no I8MM/SMMLA instruction is emitted; the real HWCAP2 probe
  records svei8mm/sve2 so "unavailable" and "available but unused"
  stay distinguishable.
- the three primitives dequantize_s8, dequantize_epilogue_bf16 and
  quantize_per_token_s8 are native v6 runner operations and
  probe-gated target entry points, bit-exact with the C1 scalar
  goldens (Q1-Q6; reserved -128, NaN/Inf, scale underflow and
  binary32 overflow fail closed).
- runner protocol v5 -> v6 and SVE256 lowering version 7 -> 8 so old
  artifacts/plans fail closed; the v5 control wire for
  iota/compare/broadcast/where is unchanged.  Batched qmatmul is an
  explicitly registered host dispatch loop over the native rank-2
  request, never a silent fallback.
- CapabilitySet declares s8s8_s32_sve_widening_sunpklo; the real
  getauxval/prctl gate cannot be forged by injected capabilities and
  cannot be disabled on a machine that passes the probe.
- 39 new focused tests cover rank2/3/4 goldens, tails, K=133144,
  +-127, -128, all-zero rows, int32 extremes, capability and metadata
  tampering, v6 wire locking, objdump widening evidence, and the
  native vs host-decode boundary.
- connected fix: _write_storage integer raw-address outputs forced
  every non-bf16 value through float(value), so an int32/int64 raw
  address raised TypeError (pre-existing known limit
  sve256_write_storage_integer_raw_address_output_preexisting_typeerror);
  the fix makes integer storage scalar-aware and extends _CTYPE plus
  the NumPy integer typestr/itemsize mapping.  This is a connected fix
  of a pre-existing defect, not a C5 regression.
